---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageFrame from '../components/PageFrame.astro';
import Masthead from '../components/Masthead.astro';
import WorkSection from '../components/WorkSection.astro';
import ActionRow from '../components/ActionRow.astro';
import TextLink from '../components/TextLink.astro';
import Dot from '../components/Dot.astro';
import Figure from '../components/Figure.astro';
import FactsList from '../components/FactsList.astro';
import CaseLead from '../components/CaseLead.astro';
import MetaLine from '../components/MetaLine.astro';
import PointsList from '../components/PointsList.astro';
import Steps from '../components/Steps.astro';
const head = `<link rel="icon" href="data:," />`;
const afterFooter = ``;
---
<Base title={"Carvingen - Gorka Molero Case Study"} description={"Carvingen is a canvas that takes an idea from a first AI image to a 3D model that carving studios in Kentucky and Missouri view in 3D glasses and carve from."}>
  <Fragment slot="head" set:html={head} />
  <PageFrame class="sheet">
    <Masthead />

      <CaseLead class="lead">
        <MetaLine class="meta eyebrow">Case · AI image to 3D to wood</MetaLine>
        <h2 class="case-title">Carvingen</h2>
        <p class="intro">Carvingen is a node canvas for AI image, video and 3D generation. Carving studios in Kentucky and Missouri put on 3D glasses, look at the model from every side and carve from it.</p>
        <MetaLine class="meta chips">Used by carving studios in Kentucky and Missouri <Dot class="dot">&middot;</Dot> From first image to 3D model on one canvas <Dot class="dot">&middot;</Dot> Public repo</MetaLine>
      </CaseLead>

      <main>
      <WorkSection class="work">
        <h2>One canvas, start to finish</h2>
        <p>To show the canvas, I made an owl landing on a log: five Nano Banana 2 images, one branch and one Meshy v6 model. Every step is a node.</p>
        <Figure class="plate">
          <div class="shot"><img src="./assets/carvingen/owl-canvas.jpg" alt="The Carvingen canvas for the owl: a chain of prompt nodes with their images, a branch, a Mesh node and a Viewer node." loading="lazy" /></div>
          <figcaption>The whole chain on one canvas, from the first image to the 3D model.</figcaption>
        </Figure>
        <Steps class="steps">
        <Figure class="step"><div class="shot"><img src="./assets/carvingen/owl-1-first-image.jpg" alt="A great horned owl landing on a log with its wings wide open." loading="lazy" /></div><figcaption>A text prompt and nothing else.</figcaption></Figure>
        <Figure class="step"><div class="shot"><img src="./assets/carvingen/owl-2-as-wood.jpg" alt="The owl as a sculpture carved from one block of pale wood." loading="lazy" /></div><figcaption>The same owl in one block of pale, unstained wood.</figcaption></Figure>
        <Figure class="step"><div class="shot"><img src="./assets/carvingen/owl-3a-wings-up.jpg" alt="The owl sculpture with its wings raised high." loading="lazy" /></div><figcaption>Wings raised higher. The one I kept.</figcaption></Figure>
        <Figure class="step"><div class="shot"><img src="./assets/carvingen/owl-3b-wings-back.jpg" alt="The owl sculpture with its wings swept back and down." loading="lazy" /></div><figcaption>Wings swept back. The other branch, still on the canvas.</figcaption></Figure>
        <Figure class="step"><div class="shot"><img src="./assets/carvingen/owl-4-simplified.jpg" alt="The owl simplified into bolder carvable planes, standing on a log." loading="lazy" /></div><figcaption>Feathers and face reduced to bolder planes a carver can cut.</figcaption></Figure>
        <Figure class="step"><div class="shot"><video controls playsinline preload="none" poster="./assets/carvingen/owl-model-poster.jpg" src="https://pub-066596d7e4fe4de2b74eac13bb03fe55.r2.dev/carvingen/owl-model.mp4" aria-label="The 3D model of the owl turning in the Carvingen viewer."></video></div><figcaption>The Meshy v6 model, turning in the viewer.</figcaption></Figure>
        </Steps>
        <p>The chosen image goes into a Mesh node and comes back as a 3D model, with GLB, FBX and USDZ files to download. The Viewer node turns it so you can check every side before carving.</p>
      </WorkSection>

      <WorkSection class="work">
        <h2>What it has made</h2>
        <p>Carvingen puts the whole path on one canvas. Before it, I made pieces like this by hand, with prompts in a chat and a separate tool for the 3D model. Two of them are here, both carved in wood.</p>

        <h3>A rider on a leaping horse</h3>
        <Steps class="steps">
        <Figure class="step"><div class="shot"><img src="./assets/carvingen/rider-01-ink-drawing.jpg" alt="An ink drawing of a woman riding a leaping horse." loading="lazy" /></div><figcaption>An ink drawing of the idea.</figcaption></Figure>
        <Figure class="step"><div class="shot"><img src="./assets/carvingen/rider-02-marble.jpg" alt="The same rider and horse as a marble sculpture." loading="lazy" /></div><figcaption>The same piece as a sculpture.</figcaption></Figure>
        <Figure class="step"><div class="shot"><video controls playsinline preload="none" poster="./assets/carvingen/woman-model-poster.jpg" src="https://pub-066596d7e4fe4de2b74eac13bb03fe55.r2.dev/carvingen/woman-model.mp4" aria-label="The 3D model of the marble rider and horse, turning."></video></div><figcaption>Its 3D model, <a href="https://www.meshy.ai/3d-models/Realistic-Marble-Statuejpg-v2-019ac0c3-eb1f-71a8-b59d-87e9ed433fa6" target="_blank" rel="noopener">on Meshy</a>.</figcaption></Figure>
        <Figure class="step"><div class="shot"><video controls playsinline preload="none" poster="./assets/carvingen/baby-model-poster.jpg" src="https://pub-066596d7e4fe4de2b74eac13bb03fe55.r2.dev/carvingen/baby-model.mp4" aria-label="The 3D model of the baby carrier, turning."></video></div><figcaption>The baby carrier as its own 3D model, <a href="https://www.meshy.ai/3d-models/Adorable-Baby-Portraitjpg-v2-019ac101-59e5-7ca3-a39f-8986b2c5ea27" target="_blank" rel="noopener">on Meshy</a>.</figcaption></Figure>
        <Figure class="step"><div class="shot"><img src="./assets/carvingen/rider-03-composite.jpg" alt="The marble rider and horse with a bronze baby carrier on her back." loading="lazy" /></div><figcaption>The carrier added on her back. This version went to 3D.</figcaption></Figure>
        <Figure class="step"><div class="shot"><video controls playsinline preload="none" poster="./assets/carvingen/horse-rider-3d-model-poster.jpg" src="https://pub-066596d7e4fe4de2b74eac13bb03fe55.r2.dev/carvingen/horse-rider-3d-model.mp4" aria-label="The 3D model of the woman on the leaping horse, turning."></video></div><figcaption>The 3D model the carvers worked from.</figcaption></Figure>
        <Figure class="step"><div class="shot"><img src="./assets/carvingen/leaping-wood.jpg" alt="The woman on the leaping horse, carved in pale wood, standing in the studio at night." loading="lazy" /></div><figcaption>The piece in the studio.</figcaption></Figure>
        <Figure class="step"><div class="shot"><video controls playsinline preload="none" poster="./assets/carvingen/leaping-carving-poster.jpg" src="https://pub-066596d7e4fe4de2b74eac13bb03fe55.r2.dev/carvingen/leaping-carving.mp4" aria-label="The woman on the leaping horse in the studio, carved in wood."></video></div><figcaption>Up close, before the finish.</figcaption></Figure>
        </Steps>

        <h3>A rider on a rearing horse</h3>
        <p>A second piece, a rider in a feathered headdress on a rearing horse.</p>
        <Steps class="steps pair">
        <Figure class="step"><div class="shot"><img src="./assets/carvingen/rearing-01-ink-drawing.jpg" alt="An ink drawing of a rider in a feathered headdress on a rearing horse." loading="lazy" /></div><figcaption>The drawing the 3D model was made from.</figcaption></Figure>
        <Figure class="step"><div class="shot"><video controls playsinline preload="none" poster="./assets/carvingen/rearing-model-poster.jpg" src="https://pub-066596d7e4fe4de2b74eac13bb03fe55.r2.dev/carvingen/rearing-model.mp4" aria-label="The 3D model of the rider on the rearing horse, turning."></video></div><figcaption>Its 3D model, <a href="https://www.meshy.ai/3d-models/IMG9310jpeg-v2-019ac138-e375-7ee8-80ad-6b96d1c296eb" target="_blank" rel="noopener">on Meshy</a>.</figcaption></Figure>
        <Figure class="step"><div class="shot"><img src="./assets/carvingen/rearing-wood.jpg" alt="The rider in a feathered headdress on a rearing horse, carved in wood, in the studio at night." loading="lazy" /></div><figcaption>The piece in the studio.</figcaption></Figure>
        <Figure class="step"><div class="shot"><video controls playsinline preload="none" poster="./assets/carvingen/rearing-carving-poster.jpg" src="https://pub-066596d7e4fe4de2b74eac13bb03fe55.r2.dev/carvingen/rearing-carving.mp4" aria-label="A carver finishing the wooden rider on the rearing horse."></video></div><figcaption>The carver finishing it.</figcaption></Figure>
        </Steps>

        <Figure class="plate">
          <div class="shot"><img src="./assets/carvingen/flatbed-both.jpg" alt="Both finished wooden pieces strapped to a flatbed truck." loading="lazy" /></div>
          <figcaption>Both pieces leaving the studio.</figcaption>
        </Figure>
      </WorkSection>

      <WorkSection class="work">
        <h2>What&rsquo;s in it</h2>
        <FactsList class="facts">
          <li><strong>Canvas</strong><span>Image, prompt, vision, video, mesh and viewer nodes. Every run is kept, any image can be a reference for the next, and every change can be undone.</span></li>
          <li><strong>Models</strong><span>Flux Kontext Pro, Nano Banana 2 and Pro, GPT Image 2, Veo 3.1, Meshy v6 and Hunyuan 3D, all through fal.</span></li>
          <li><strong>3D</strong><span>GLB, FBX and USDZ files, a viewer, and scripts that rig, animate and pack characters for games.</span></li>
          <li><strong>Why a canvas</strong><span>A chat loses which image came from which. On the canvas you branch, compare and go back. It is a node workflow in the way ComfyUI is, built to take a concept all the way to a 3D model.</span></li>
        </FactsList>
        <ActionRow class="actions"><TextLink class="button primary" href="https://github.com/gorkamolero/carvingen" target="_blank" rel="noopener">View source</TextLink></ActionRow>
      </WorkSection>
      </main>
  </PageFrame>
  <Fragment slot="after-footer" set:html={afterFooter} />
</Base>
